Probably not, since I cheated once, but in a really weird way.

I used to play nethack some years ago, but without having read spoilers
I never came far, usually died of something like soldier ants or angry
shopkeepers before level 10.
The spoilers helped a lot and made me more interested in the game, I´m
still amazed about the vast number of gameplay detials and
possibilities.
Fighters were easier and I got two valkyries through the quest, but the
wizards and healers still kept dying, until one elven wizard called
Asaniel simply refused to. He learned some good spells like magic
missile and create monster, silver dragon mail from a magic lamp and
speed boots from a armor shop, and the BoH from Sokoban.
In Minetown he served his god Ahnur well, got Magicbane and stealth, and
finally the great moment when Arioch looked down upon him and gave him
some resistances and the Finger of Death, and he felt really cool and
evil.
Not experienced enough for Neferet, he went down. Medusa´s lake was
frozen by cones of cold, but below her horrors lurked: a Master Lich.
The lich laughed about the death finger, and Asaniels´s other attempts
him, but magic and cold resistant he was equally protected against the
lich, and Magicbane absorbed most curses except one. From unburdened to
overtaxed? What is going on? Get out some holy water, luckily it was not
destroyed by the bag. The battle went on and the level was almost full
of monsters, my energy was always low until I remembered the idea and
made statues of the lich and his pet mind flayer.
Found some potions and entered the Quest. The Dark one proved out to be
ridiculous, since he slept quietly and never noticed what spell hit him.
The Exes were really useful, since now he could really fight like a
wizard instead like a fighter with some magic spells. But what was that?
That knowledge of spells could fade was a new experience to me, so bad
were the other wizards. But I still knew where the spellboks were safely
kept.
Somewhere he good teleportitis from a tin of nymph meat (didn´t know
that tins could do that too), but found a ring of teleport control not
much later.
Cleared the castle, ate a black dragon, and wished for a blessed magic
marker, gauntlets of dexterity and a helm of brilliance. I wrote some
spells to enchant and partly fireproof my armor and Magicbane, bought
some more protection, and entered Gehennom. (the first time for me
outside of debugmode).
Gehenomm was rather easy, fired away with magic missile against the
demons and finger of death against the rest, the minotaurs and
mindflayers rarely hat a chance to hit him, the attacks of the liches
and demon lords ware no danger. The exception was Juiblex, but he could
cast cure sickness and eventually managed to kill it from inside. The
vampires sometimes managed to suck a level, so the level remained <20,
but Vlad was no problem either. Magic mapping and teleport control
protect well against maze boredom, too.
Except for the deppest level. He had to do something really unchaotic
and map each square with a single coin, a dwarf would have gone crazy
looking at the map. Did I say unchaotic? Oh, several elvenkings, ogre
lords and giants got into the missile and death rays, but who cares?

Then hybris struck him. Going up to reread spellbooks and buy candles
before attacking the Wizard of Yendor, he went greedy for a better
weapon like Stormbringer. Killed the priest of Molock in the Valley,
tried to convert it. Moloch laughed at this attempt and rejected the
sacrifice.. Panicking, he went to minetown and offered some corpse.
You have a feeling of inadequacy.
Now I panicked too. Thought an angry god would never allow him on the
Astral plane, remembering from the tournament a endling "escaped in
celestial disgrace", I decided to forfeit the game and try to continue
with savescumming. Saved it and started desperate tries. "Create
monster" never brought monsters which pleased him, even white unicorns,
or else the corpses could not be lifted. Remembered that once I
reconciled a angry chaotic god by an ettin, I used my remaining wishes
from the wand and a magic lamp on ettin corpses. Anhur only was slightly
mollified. Tried once again, orgot to recharge the magic marker, so I
stood there without any wishes, without a magic marker and an angry god.

Then I took this game with the worst outcome (all remaining wishes and
markers spent for something useless, Anhur still angry), so I would not
be any better off than without the cheat, and play it straight to the
end.
 
Entered the Wizard´s tower with help of some rings I found in Gehennom
(levitation, conflict and slow digestion), started the ceremony and get
the amulet. Rodney was no problem, I always used finger of death against
him as soon as he reappeared, knowing that if he managed to steal the
Eyes or Magicbane I would have no chance against him. Teleported my way
up, killed Orcus on the way who blocked the stairway, identified the
Amulet again.
On the elementary plains I always used the rings of conflict and
levitation and ran away from the monsters searching for the portals.
Water took long since I ran aimlessly around from bubble to bubble until
the amulet felt hot, on Fire only an staring archon was dangerous which
i teleported away (read the trick here)
"Thy desire for conflict shall be fulfilled", I was greeted on the
Astral Plane, and soon realized that this was too hard for me, all the
ascension posts had far better stats. Death decreased my lifeforce much
further, but somehow I managed to run away from him and found an altar
Luckily it was the chaotic one.
Well, this is no real ascension since I broke the rules once, but
reading all the spoilers which is inside the rules makes a far greater
difference.
Now i know that most of the information can be gathered from within the
game, from collecting all the Oracle´s answers and experimenting a lot,
but I would not have the patience for that.
Still the game was great fun, and thanks to those who wrote the game and
also all the stuff in the group nd on the sites, I will try to do it
once proper, but with a lawful fighter for change.

